    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T14:58:43Z",
    "body": "Fix ready, but I can't open a PR: `mkinney/Camcraft` is no longer in NeoTech/Camcraft's fork network. GitHub now lists its parent as `linuxguy123/Camcraft`, and PR creation fails with \"head invalid\". Here is the patch (pinned by a new `warned_moves::a_holder_hit_names_its_move`, 3/3 green, clippy clean). It's also on `mkinney/Camcraft` branch `issue/458-holderhit-match` (88f7c390):\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/crates/app/src/warned_moves.rs b/crates/app/src/warned_moves.rs\nindex 985f03b2..67158ce2 100644\n--- a/crates/app/src/warned_moves.rs\n+++ b/crates/app/src/warned_moves.rs\n@@ -29,7 +29,8 @@ pub fn moves_named(w: &Warning) -> [Option<usize>; 2] {\n         | Warning::FixtureHit { at, .. }\n         | Warning::NonFinite { at }\n         | Warning::Envelope { at, .. }\n-        | Warning::Scallop { at, .. } => [Some(*at), None],\n+        | Warning::Scallop { at, .. }\n+        | Warning::HolderHit { at, .. } => [Some(*at), None],\n         Warning::RestUnjudged { .. } => [None, None],\n     }\n }\n```\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
